db/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205038 #edb/ref 1061 476522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205038 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "15db0382-7d51-5840-b3da-75384a89354d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205038 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186205207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1061 476523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8211e280-4fa1-564c-9189-09c44ee53dde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1061 476526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "16595ce8-f055-561b-9a7f-397923fee1b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205041 #edb/ref 1061 476529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205041 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eddfa8ae-b5d6-5ef0-ba45-f6c57207ae16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205041 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1064 "Some linear equations can have **no solutions.** This means there is no value of $x$ that can be substituted into the equation to give a true statement.\n\nFor example, let's consider the following equation:\n\n$$\nx+1 = x\n$$\n\nLet's attempt to solve this equation. We start by subtracting $x$ from both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =x \\\\ x+1\\,-\\,x & =x\\,-\\,x \\\\ (x-x)+1 & =(x-x) \\\\ 0+1 & =0 \\\\ 1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the final equation, $1=0,$ is always **false**. In other words, there is no value of $x$ that we can substitute to make the equation true. \n\nTherefore, our equation has no solutions." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1065 11390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ae552721-c050-5d83-9cfc-347accbc894b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n7qx = -5,\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solutions, what is the value of $q?$\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax = b{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7q}_{\\large a} \\ x = \\underbrace{-5}_{\\large b}\n$$\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\na = 7q, \\qquad b = -5.\n$$\n\nWe know that an equation of the form $ax=b$ with $b \\neq 0$ has no solutions when $a = 0.$\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n7q = 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7q & =0 \\\\ \\frac{7q}{7} & =\\frac{0}{7} \\\\ q & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the equation $7qx = -5$ has no solutions if $q = 0.$\n\n**Note:** The constant $q$ in this problem is sometimes called a **parameter.**" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1065 13402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d31382b3-ae61-5a9e-a3bf-53f71f939a5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1067 "Problems Involving Unknown Parameters" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1064 "In general, suppose we have an equation in the variable $x$ of the form \n\n$$\nax = b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $a$ and $b$ are constants, and\n\n- $b$ is *not* equal to zero, which we write as $b \\neq 0.$\n\nThen, if $a = 0,$ the equation has **no solutions.**\n\nIndeed, by substituting $a = 0$ into $ax=b,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ax & =b \\\\ (0)x & =b \\\\ 0 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a *contradiction* (i.e., a statement that's always false) because we were told that $b \\neq 0.$ Therefore, the equation has no solution." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1065 13428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8a5cc3be-1b56-5e46-8944-f75697b65b59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1067 "Conditions for an Equation To Have No Solutions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295501 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{9}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295501 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295501 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "298bad1f-9367-5a05-95d2-933a09daee2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295623 #edb/ref 1080 "-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295623 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295623 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3dad73b7-975d-5246-83b7-9657d612712e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295682 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295682 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295682 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "488785de-3552-5c44-b37c-f80db84151a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296138 #edb/ref 1080 "-9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296138 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296138 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a52921f6-35e3-5fd6-831b-5c76a68fe597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296286 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296286 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296286 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c10c0188-b833-5221-be57-af73a4dae17b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296559 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296559 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296559 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f34978c9-f088-5aab-b438-960ba47ee1ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296784 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186295682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296784 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296784 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296784 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186295682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296784 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4f518425-6bb3-513e-9a2f-cd6d4cd2d157" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296994 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 1759218629